-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What you may do
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

As long as you follow section 2, you may, free of charge:

  a. Use. Download, install and use official AltLoad builds on devices you
     own or are authorised to manage, for your own personal, non-commercial
     purposes.

  b. Build. Build the Software from this source, including in your own
     GitHub fork using GitHub Actions, and install that build on your own
     devices, for the same purposes.

  c. Fork and contribute. Fork the repository on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms
     of Service allow, and modify your fork in order to propose changes back
     to AltLoad. By sending a contribution (for example a pull request), you
     agree that mirazbakis may use, change and distribute it as part of the
     Software under this license or any later version of it.

  d. Read and refer. Read and study the source, and quote short parts of it
     with credit when discussing or reviewing AltLoad.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. What you may not do without written permission
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  a. Redistribute the Software or builds of it, modified or not, outside of
     GitHub's own fork feature. Link people to the official repository,
     releases or website instead.

  b. Publish a modified version as a separate app or project, or present one
     as the official AltLoad.

  c. Use the Software commercially: sell it or builds of it, charge for
     access to it, include it in a paid product, subscription, signing,
     "certificate" or sideloading service or app store, put downloads behind
     ads, link shorteners or donations, or use it to provide a paid service.

  d. Use the AltLoad name or logo for anything other than referring to
     AltLoad accurately, or in a way that suggests endorsement.

  e. Remove or change this license, the copyright notice or
     THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in any copy of the Software, including builds.

  f. Use the Software to install, distribute or facilitate apps you don't
     have the right to use, such as pirated or cracked apps, or to access
     devices or accounts you aren't authorised to access.

To ask for permission, open an issue at https://github.com/mirazbakis/AltLoad
or contact mirazbakis through GitHub.

If you break these terms, every permission in section 1 ends automatically.
It is restored if you fix the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it.

